@anon.24b545d8b979284340e25a03af0d8ae8.219 = private unnamed_addr constant [564 x i8] c"Specifies the version of Python that will be used to analyze the source code. The version should be specified as a string in the format `M.m` where `M` is the major version and `m` is the minor (e.g. `\223.0\22` or `\223.6\22`). If a version is provided, ty will generate errors if the source code makes use of language features that are not supported in that version. It will also understand conditionals based on comparisons with `sys.version_info`, such as are commonly found in typeshed to reflect the differing contents of the standard library across Python versions.", align 1
@anon.24b545d8b979284340e25a03af0d8ae8.220 = private unnamed_addr constant [453 x i8] c"Specifies the target platform that will be used to analyze the source code. If specified, ty will understand conditions based on comparisons with `sys.platform`, such as are commonly found in typeshed to reflect the differing contents of the standard library across platforms.\0A\0AIf no platform is specified, ty will use the current platform: - `win32` for Windows - `darwin` for macOS - `android` for Android - `ios` for iOS - `linux` for everything else", align 1
@anon.24b545d8b979284340e25a03af0d8ae8.221 = private unnamed_addr constant [208 x i8] c"List of user-provided paths that should take first priority in the module resolution. Examples in other type checkers are mypy's `MYPYPATH` environment variable, or pyright's `stubPath` configuration setting.", align 1
@anon.24b545d8b979284340e25a03af0d8ae8.222 = private unnamed_addr constant [214 x i8] c"Optional path to a \22typeshed\22 directory on disk for us to use for standard-library types. If this is not provided, we will fallback to our vendored typeshed stubs for the stdlib, bundled as a zip file in the binary", align 1
